# 27B environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in a key to enable the imagery renderer.
# Everything EXCEPT the final 3D render (geocoding, building/height lookup,
# elevation + heading math, caching, metrics, and the full UI) works with no
# key. With no key set, the app shows the honest "imagery source not configured"
# state — never a placeholder or simulated scene.

# Google Maps Platform API key with the "Map Tiles API" enabled
# (Photorealistic 3D Tiles). This gates the CesiumJS renderer.
#
# Get one at https://console.cloud.google.com/ -> APIs & Services -> Credentials,
# then enable "Map Tiles API". Restrict the key to your deploy origin(s).
#
# COST NOTE: Photorealistic 3D Tiles is free to ~1,000 tile-events/month, then
# ~$6/1,000. At ~4 renders/address that's ~250 free addresses/month. The app
# caches aggressively (address-keyed) to stay under this cap. Do NOT exceed the
# free cap in production without an explicit cost decision.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=
